title: StartRJ
// Corresponds to Scene 2 in the narrative script
// This scene is from Jovan's POV
// The cousin is the only character present in the scene
---
<<declare $lover1Name = "Jovan">>
<<declare $cousinName = "Sasha">>
<<changeBG 0>>
<<zeroChar>>

{$lover1Name} is running around his dining room frantically. 
He's looking in drawers and behind furniture. 
He gets more and more desperate as he mutters to himself.
{$lover1Name}: I must have misplaced it. 
{$lover1Name}: I must have picked it up and put it somewhere. 
{$lover1Name}: It's fine, no one else has-

<<oneChar>>
<<changeSprite 1 0>>
{$cousinName} walks into the kitchen and sits at the table with a slice of chocolate cake.
<<lighten 1>>
{$cousinName}: Are you looking for something?
<<darken 1>>

{$lover1Name} freezes before forcing himself to appear calm.
{$lover1Name}: Not really. Just a pen.

<<lighten 1>>
{$cousinName}: Not really? Or just a pen?
<<darken 1>>

{$lover1Name}'s heart beats faster.
<<lighten 1>>
{$cousinName}: (Sighs) Or was it a letter?
<<darken 1>>

{$lover1Name} feels his eyes go wide.
{$lover1Name}: Why would you think-

<<lighten 1>>
{$cousinName} holds up the envelope and waves it in the air.
{$cousinName}: I found this by your favorite bench in the old park.
<<darken 1>>

{$lover1Name} rushes forward and grabs the letter. Then he steps back, but stops when {$cousinName} speaks.

<<lighten 1>>
{$cousinName}: {$lover1Name}. What's in the letter?
<<darken 1>>

{$lover1Name}: Uh, what do you mean?

<<lighten 1>>
{$cousinName} puts down his fork.
{$cousinName}: A letter with no return address thats clearly filled with shredded paper was left in a park for you to find. 
{$cousinName}: On top of that, you won't tell me what's in the letter.
<<darken 1>>

{$lover1Name}: I mean, we all have our secrets, right?

<<lighten 1>>
{$cousinName}: Secrets are dangerous right now.
<<darken 1>>

{$lover1Name} felt his expression drop into fear.
{$lover1Name}: I know. But its nothing, I promise.

<<lighten 1>>
Picking up the fork and shaking his head, {$cousinName} gives up.
{$cousinName}: Fine. But you'll tell me if it's something I should worry about.
<<darken 1>>

A smile blooms on {$lover1Name}'s face.
{$lover1Name}: Of course!

There's an awkward pause. 

<<lighten 1>>
{$cousinName}: Well? Are you going to open it?
<<darken 1>>

{$lover1Name}: I will. I just, uh, need some privacy.

<<lighten 1>>
{$cousinName}: Fine. I'll let you be suspicious in peace.
<<darken 1>>
{$cousinName} leaves the room.
<<zeroChar>>

{$lover1Name} dumps the pieces of the letter and begins to assemble it before he even sits down.
===
